            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0200" n="1034" xml:id="pg1034"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9482</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-03T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 3, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2392. For Dresel [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 73. French desire inter-Allied committee, Paris, to send joint resolution to
                    S[ociété] S[uisse de] S[urveillance Economique], Berne, that unless necessary
                    steps to include some names of S.S.S. members in Swiss black list are completed
                    before a certain date, Paris committee will compile list and include S.S.S.
                    members engaged in contraband trade giving S.S.S. appeal from decisions. French
                    consider such inclusion will not violate article 3 of S.S.S. agreement. Have
                    telegraphed McFadden,
                    Paris, to communicate with you and determine whether you approve this proposed
                    resolution before acting. Telegraph your opinion Washington also.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
